From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:21:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve source-layer winners and the complete reindex
 handoff

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the promoted
series (tree ea1281f880e7535e3d87725be0156a8e38fc2fb2), the independent
inactive-read guard and experimental cluster-search patches through 0005.

Rationale: source layers publish 2048 eight-key blocks as well as 512 keys.
A threshold derived only from the immediate winners cannot preserve that
later reindex domain. Seed enough distinct blocks, derive a conservative
2047-ordinary-block threshold, and retain the global last visible cluster.
Restore retained native scores to original positions for the unchanged
native source block selector. Small planned domains use the native source
path directly, without measuring it as a new reference.

Quality: preserve both immediate keys and source block IDs/counts. The
mandatory last block is retained independently of its score. Equality always
survives. Native MXFP4 scoring and block/key tie rules are unchanged.

Tests: exact source keys, candidate blocks/counts, compact BF16 score bits,
a following native reindex query, changing graph visibility, cache mutation
and sanitizers are required. Hardware execution remains pending.

Upstream status: local experimental candidate, not submitted upstream.

The restoration kernel writes every dense score once through a shared
cluster-offset map; it needs no ATen fill or racing scatter initialization.
The original Active cap safely covers both cluster and sampled-key counts.
